 |-
 | Data
 | {{Type|Prefixed Optional}} {{Type|NBT}}
 | Entry data. If omitted, sourced from the selected [[Java Edition protocol/Registries#Known packs negotiation|known packs]].
 |}

The ordering of the entries in the Entries array defines the numeric IDs that they will be assigned to, starting from 0 and counting upwards. It is essential to maintain consistency between server and client, since many parts of the protocol reference these entries by their ID. The client will disconnect upon receiving a reference to a non-existing entry.

The NBT data of registry entries has the same structure as their definitions in [[data packs]], but [[NBT format#Conversion from JSON|represented in NBT instead of JSON]]. The format for each registry is defined in [[Java Edition protocol/Registries#List of synchronized registries]].

