Starting from version 1.5, “painting mode” is available for use in inventory windows. It is done by picking up a stack of something (more than 1 item), then holding {{mouse|left}}, {{mouse|right}} or {{mouse|middle}} and dragging the held stack over empty (or same type in case of right button) slots. In that case client sends the following to the server after the mouse button release (omitting the first pickup packet, which is sent as usual):

# packet with mode 5, slot -999, button (0 for left | 4 for right);
# packet for every slot painted on, mode is still 5, button (1 | 5);
# packet with mode 5, slot -999, button (2 | 6);

If any of the painting packets other than the “progress” ones are sent out of order (for example, a start, some slots, then another start; or a left-click in the middle) the painting status will be reset.

